## 4. Bug #4 — RSS Samples Not Saved ✅ FIXED

**Symptom:** Time chip showed correct RSS time, but "RSS samples" in the Show Settings modal were empty.

**Root cause:** `recordMatchedRssObservation` had two over-strict guards rejecting samples:
- `implausibly-ahead-of-anilist`: rejected if `episode > nextEpisode + 2`
- `older-than-history`: rejected if `episode < newestHistoryEpisode`

The display time bypassed these guards (saved directly from `item.latestReleaseDate`), but `entry.history` did not — hence "it records something" (the time) but no samples.

**Fix applied (already in current file):** Rewrote `recordMatchedRssObservation`:
- Removed both `implausibly-ahead-of-anilist` and `older-than-history` guards
- Added fallback episode logic (`nextEpisode - 1` when `matchedEpisode` is null, matching the older working version)
- Kept `beyond-total` guard and `ignored` guard (for "Drop latest")
- Kept basic validity checks (day, time, timestamp)

The fixed function currently in the code:

```javascript
function recordMatchedRssObservation(item, entry) {
    const episode = episodeNumberFromToken(item?.matchedEpisode);
    const currentDay = String(item?.latestReleaseDay || "");
    const currentTime = String(item?.latestReleaseTime || "");
    const releaseAtMs = Number(item?.latestReleaseDate);

    // Basic validity: need a day, time, and a timestamp.
    if (!WEEKDAYS.includes(currentDay) || !isValidTime(currentTime) ||
        !Number.isFinite(releaseAtMs) || releaseAtMs <= 0) {
        return { saved: false, changed: false, reason: "incomplete" };
    }

    // Fallback episode matching the working version's logic:
    // if matchedEpisode is null, use displayEpisode - 1 (the just-aired episode).
    let resolvedEpisode = episode;
    if (resolvedEpisode === null) {
        const nextEp = episodeNumberFromToken(item?.aniListNextEpisode);
        if (nextEp !== null && nextEp > 1) resolvedEpisode = nextEp - 1;
    }
    if (resolvedEpisode === null) {
        return { saved: false, changed: false, reason: "incomplete" };
    }

    // Keep the beyond-total guard (prevents genuinely invalid data)
    const totalEpisode = episodeNumberFromToken(item?.totalEpisodeNumber);
    if (totalEpisode !== null && resolvedEpisode > totalEpisode) {
        return { saved: false, changed: false, reason: "beyond-total" };
    }

    // REMOVED: implausibly-ahead-of-anilist guard
    // REMOVED: older-than-history guard

    entry.history = Array.isArray(entry.history) ? entry.history : [];

    // Keep the ignored-episode guard (respects user's "Drop latest" action)
    const ignoredRssEpisode = episodeNumberFromToken(entry.ignoredRssEpisode);
    if (ignoredRssEpisode !== null && ignoredRssEpisode === resolvedEpisode) {
        return { saved: false, changed: false, reason: "ignored" };
    }

    const episodeToken = rssEpisodeToken(resolvedEpisode);
    const sample = {
        day: currentDay,
        time: currentTime,
        mins: toMinutes(currentTime),
        episode: episodeToken,
        releaseAtMs,
        offsetMs: Number(state.rssTimeOffsetMs) || 0
    };

    const existingHistoryIndex = entry.history.findIndex(
        historySample => episodeNumberFromToken(historySample?.episode) === resolvedEpisode
    );
    let changed = false;
    if (existingHistoryIndex >= 0) {
        const existing = entry.history[existingHistoryIndex] || {};
        if (existing.day !== sample.day || existing.time !== sample.time ||
            Number(existing.releaseAtMs) !== Number(sample.releaseAtMs) ||
            Number(existing.offsetMs || 0) !== Number(sample.offsetMs || 0)) {
            entry.history[existingHistoryIndex] = sample;
            changed = true;
        }
    } else {
        entry.history.push(sample);
        if (entry.history.length > 3) entry.history.shift();
        changed = true;
    }

    const storedLatestRelease = Number(entry.latestReleaseDate);
    if (!Number.isFinite(storedLatestRelease) || releaseAtMs >= storedLatestRelease) {
        entry.latestReleaseDate = releaseAtMs;
    }
    if (changed) entry.updatedAt = new Date().toISOString();
    return { saved: true, changed, sample };
}
